SCORED ON w, NOT ON B/(A+B). The EXA ratio's denominator carries a fitted intercept far noisier than the slope it is added to, and that intercept goes NEGATIVE in two of the 2026-09-10 session's arms, so a residency effect of a few per cent in the slope arrives in the ratio as a sign flip. w is the same slope over a byte count from moe.spec and a rate the caller names: no fitted level and no intercept. The per-cent noise figures the session-3 analysis quotes for w are ITS figures and are in no committed file here, so they are not printed as this page's; the spread this design is actually powered against is the line below, which says ASSUMED or says which of this run's own cells it measured.

ridge 151.427 Op/B, measured on this device: NVIDIA H200 (measured), 663.0 TFLOP/s bf16 over 4378.0 GB/s (triad pattern); calibrated 2026-09-21 at 81f80b7b. Used ONLY by V4, to ask whether each cell's MEASURED marginal arithmetic intensity is below it. No claim here is scored against a roof.
the concurrency model predicts +0.0561 in ln w per doubling of residency over 2 to 16 blocks/SM at 132 SMs over 63 MB of L2; NO GATE IS SCORED ON ITS LEVEL and C2 quotes bR against it only to give the size a unit.

NOT A READOUT. Everything above is arithmetic over this repo's calibration and vLLM's resource model. NOT A PRODUCTION CLAIM: BLOCK_SIZE_K 32 and 128 are settings vLLM ships for other shapes, and this grid is chosen to separate two mechanisms, not to recommend a tile. NOT RUN: no cell below has been timed.

## The plan

model        mixtral-8x7b E=8 k=2 bf16 (2 B/element)
pinned       BLOCK_SIZE_M=64 BLOCK_SIZE_N=64 GROUP_SIZE_M=1 num_warps=4  (num_stages and BLOCK_SIZE_K are the sweep)
cells        8: 1x32, 2x32, 3x32, 6x32, 3x64, 4x64, 2x128, 3x128
treads       8 exactly-full tile stacks per cell, r = 64..512 rows per expert, T = 256..2048 tokens
repeats      15 round-robin passes per cell
timing       300 ms of warmup under load, then 3 trial(s) of 200 ms of kernel time each, L2 flush ON; the instrument sizes its own iteration count
timings      960 (8 cells x 8 treads x 15 reps)
estimate     864 s of GPU at what the instrument charges (warmup + trials x budget per timing), excluding compiles and allocation
not priced   the two terms that figure leaves out, with what is known about each rather than a shrug. COMPILES: at most 8 x 8 = 64 distinct Triton specialisations, and probably 8 -- the kernel's constexprs are the tile, and every token count on this ladder is a multiple of 16, so the divisibility-by-16 specialisation key does not move across the treads. The COMPILE CENSUS pays the first one per cell before the metered loop and prints the count it actually built. ALLOCATION: the expert weight set is drawn ONCE, not once per tread -- moe.reference.torch_ref.make_inputs caches it on (model, dtype, seed, device, scale), which this arm never moves -- so the 960 rebuilds redraw only the activations, at most 17 MB each.
