REFUSED: the kernel probe read no n_regs for 8 of 8 cell(s): 1x32, 2x128, 2x32, 3x128, 3x32, 3x64, 4x64, 6x32 (probe note: vLLM exposes no fused_moe_kernel with a Triton cache under either known path, so the compiled shared memory could not be read). Residency is min(by_smem, by_threads, by_blocks, by_regs) and only the first depends on BLOCK_SIZE_K, so without n_regs every cell carries an upper BOUND and V3 reads UNKNOWN, which makes the whole page INVALID after the metered loop has been paid for. The probe reads `n_regs` off the compiled kernel object and `shared` off its metadata, and either can be absent on a Triton the probe does not know. Nothing was timed.
